NEARS-1775 task_bug: ui_freshness_probe NEVER succeeds against a real running
debug app — the VM-service log-line grep pattern does not match what Flutter
actually writes to `adb logcat`.

scripts/app-nav/uinav.sh:671 (as shipped):
  vmurl="$(adb -s "$s" logcat -d 2>/dev/null | grep -aF "Dart VM Service" | grep -aoE 'http://[^[:space:]]+/' | tail -1)"

grep -aF "Dart VM Service" is a CASE-SENSITIVE fixed-string match for capital
"Service". The real on-device logcat line (Flutter 3.41.9, UserApp,
com.izzes.nears, emulator-5554) is:

  08-21 01:25:39.392 20936 21012 I flutter : The Dart VM service is listening on http://127.0.0.1:42231/qULwQdsBl-g=/

— lowercase "service", and a different surrounding phrase ("is listening on"
vs the "available at:" wording assumed in the function's own comment/error
text at uinav.sh:645/673). The test fixtures in uinav.test.sh encode the SAME
wrong wording ("A Dart VM Service on sdk is available at: ...") — that string
never appears on a real device, only in the fixture, so the automated suite
is green while the shipped function is 100% non-functional against a live
device.

Independent verification, live device emulator-5554, com.izzes.nears
(package resolves and pid resolves cleanly both times — the bug is isolated
to the VM-service line grep):

$ adb -s emulator-5554 logcat -d | grep -acF "VM Service"   # capital S, what the code greps for
0
$ adb -s emulator-5554 logcat -d | grep -acF "VM service"   # lowercase s, what Flutter actually emits
6

As-shipped repro (pid 21567, fresh app, freshly reinstalled, definitely
running and definitely a debug build with an active VM service — confirmed by
the same line existing in logcat under the lowercase-s spelling):

$ source scripts/app-nav/uinav.sh
$ adb -s emulator-5554 shell pidof com.izzes.nears
21567
$ ui_freshness_probe -s emulator-5554; echo "RC=$?"
ui_freshness_probe: emulator-5554 NOT ASSERTED: no 'Dart VM Service … available at:' line in the log buffer for pid 21567 (com.izzes.nears) - not a debug build, buffer rotated, or the VM service was never announced
RC=2

This blocks AC1 and AC2 outright: the probe can never emit its one JSON
record against a real running debug app, on the exact host/emulator/Flutter
combination this repo's own pool uses.

Proof the REST of the mechanism (pid-bind, adb forward, curl->getVM, pid
cross-check, JSON emit, forward teardown hygiene) is otherwise sound: a
scratch copy of uinav.sh with ONLY line 671's grep changed from
`grep -aF "Dart VM Service"` to `grep -aiF "Dart VM Service"` (case-insensitive,
no other change) succeeds end-to-end against the SAME live process:

$ source /tmp/.../uinav-patched.sh   # -aiF fix only, no other change
$ ui_freshness_probe -s emulator-5554
{"timestamp": "2026-08-20T21:26:56Z", "pid": 20936, "build_symbols": "isolates/4761369954348891"}
$ adb -s emulator-5554 shell pidof com.izzes.nears
20936

Suggested fix: change `grep -aF "Dart VM Service"` to a case-insensitive match
(`grep -aiF`) or match the actual on-device wording, and correct the fixture
in uinav.test.sh (currently pinned to the wrong string, which is how this
shipped green) plus the doc/error-string wording ("... available at:" ->
"... is listening on" or a wording-agnostic match).
